### 📦 Git LFS Setup (Important!)

Since the file is 8.1 GB, you'll need **Git Large File Storage (LFS)**:

```bash
# Install Git LFS
sudo apt install git-lfs

# Initialize Git LFS in your repo
git lfs install

# Track the .qcow2 file
git lfs track "*.qcow2"

# Add the tracking file
git add .gitattributes

# Commit and push
git add debian11-miashs.qcow2
git commit -m "Add Debian 11 VM with Marionnet"
git push
```

**Note:** GitHub LFS has storage limits on free accounts (1 GB storage, 1 GB bandwidth per month). For an 8 GB file, you might need:
- GitHub Pro account, OR
- Host the file on Google Drive/Dropbox and link to it in the README

